2026-03-26 13:34:49 - Agent_20260326132703 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 17 CodeQL queries across 6 files focusing on path traversal vulnerabilities. Key findings:

TRUE POSITIVES (4):
1. StaticFileHandler.sanitizePath (lines 275-282): String-based dot-segment checks without URL-decoding, bypassable with %2e%2e encoded sequences
2. StaticFileHandler.locateFile (lines 98-106): No containment check after Path.resolve() - absolute path injection via double-slash in URI (e.g. /static//etc/passwd) bypasses sanitizePath entirely since sanitizePath doesn't block non-dot absolute paths
3. FileSystemBucket.getObject/deleteObject/findObject (lines 193-215): Missing containment checks present in putObject - inconsistent protection allows path traversal for reads and deletes
4. FileSaveHandler.parseObjectName (lines 85-95): Single-pass regex traversal cleanup bypassable with patterns like '....//etc/passwd' when allowRemoteProvidedSubdirectory=true

FALSE POSITIVES (4):
1. BackupCli line 154: startsWith() on JVM process display names, not file paths
2. AngularHandler line 96: locateFile() used for routing existence check only; actual serving goes through sanitizePath via super.handle()
3. FileSystemBucket.putObject lines 146-149: Correct canonicalize-then-check pattern (getCanonicalPath().startsWith())
4. FileSystemBucket lines 84-85: AtomicLong/AtomicInteger counter operations, not path operations

MANUAL REVIEW (1):
1. FileBasedConfigurationResolver line 26: normalize() without containment check, but name parameter likely internal/trusted - needs caller analysis to confirm exploitability
